 medal came from the blue. Lindland was also not well known, but would win a silver medal at the 2001 World Championships and then turned to mixed martial arts, competing with multiple groups in that fighting sport in the United States. Yli-Hannuksela would improve to a silver medal in this class at the 2004 Olympics."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Classification Points", :class "footnote"} "CP"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Technical Points", :class "footnote"} "TP"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "8"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/95079"} "Murat Kardanov"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/RUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/RUS.png"}] "RUS"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "19"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/95174"} "Matt Lindland"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "4"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/58019"} "Marko Yli-Hannuksela"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FIN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FIN.png"}] "FIN"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {:class "bib"} "15"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/ath